# Build context for all three images is the repository root, so this file is
# what keeps the host's working tree out of them.
#
# It is not an optimisation. Without the node_modules rule the frontend image
# does not build at all: `COPY frontend/ ./` lands the host's pnpm symlink farm
# on top of the real directories the `dependencies` stage installed, and
# buildkit stops with "cannot copy to non-directory". Without the .env rules a
# developer's real credentials are baked into an image layer, where they stay
# readable after any later `rm`.

# --- dependency trees ------------------------------------------------------
# Installed inside the image from the lockfiles. The host copies are built for
# the host's platform, so even when they copy cleanly they are wrong.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/.pnpm-store

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# An image layer is not a secret store. Configuration reaches the containers
# through compose, at run time.
# `**/` and not a bare `.env`: there are three of these — at the root, in
# backend/, and in frontend/ — and a root-anchored pattern would only catch the
# first.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
secrets/

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------
# Produced inside the image. A stale host copy shadowing a fresh build is the
# kind of bug that only shows up in production.
frontend/build
frontend/.react-router
backend/dist
backend/build
**/*.egg-info

# --- caches ----------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.import_linter_cache
**/.cache
**/.turbo
**/.vite

# --- test and tooling artefacts --------------------------------------------
frontend/playwright-report
frontend/test-results
frontend/test-results-parity
frontend/parity-output
**/coverage
**/htmlcov
**/.coverage
**/.nyc_output
backups/

# --- repository metadata ---------------------------------------------------
# .git is the big one: it is often larger than the source and nothing in any
# image reads it.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# --- things no image needs -------------------------------------------------
docs/
observability/
infrastructure/
deploy/helm/
scripts/
tests/
**/*.md
!README.md
Taskfile.yml
